}}|subdivision_type1=[[Communities of Balisca|Community]]|subdivision_name1={{flag|Cerdanya}}|area_km2=21219.89|population_census=1,265,282|population_census_year=2020|regional_languages=|common_languages={{W|Aranese dialect|Cerdanyan Beron}}, [[Baliscano]], {{W|Catalan language|Volisanian}} and {{W|Mapuche language|Walldungu}}|cctld=.wln|mapsize=280px}}'''Wüñülelfün''' ({{Literal translation|west wind land}}) is a [[Regions of Balisca|region]] of [[Cerdanya]], within the [[Balisca|Baliscan Confederation]], located at the extreme western end of the [[Tinguirirican Peninsula|Tinguiririca Peninsula]]. It contains the westernmost point of mainland Balisca, [[Pelullafken]]. It borders [[Provence]] and [[Muntanya]] to the north/northeast and [[Pigüe]] to the south.

Wüñülelfün's economy, because of its important geographic location, is mainly based on a well-developed service sector, especially commerce, tourism, and trading. The completion of the [[Pirihueico Canal|Pirihueico Seaway]] in the 1890s, followed by the expansion of military installations after the [[Camboriú War]] has given rise to an economic revitalization. 

